Description: pipeline: simple: autofocus defaults and settling for camera apps
 For camera applications that use libcamera through PipeWire or GStreamer
 and never set AfMode:
  - continuous AF is the default mode when the sensor has a focus lens
    (LIBCAMERA_SIMPLE_AF_MODE=manual|auto|continuous overrides it);
  - a continuous scan starts on the first request after every start();
  - a FocusFoM is only used from a frame at least two frames after the
    one whose statistics moved the lens;
  - LIBCAMERA_SIMPLE_AF_RANGE=<min>-<max> narrows the scan to a module's
    calibrated range, manual focus keeps the full range;
  - the soft IPA divides the FocusFoM by the mean luminance, so that an
    exposure change alone does not restart a continuous scan.
 .
 Patch 4/4 of the libcamera autofocus series of iceland-mainline
 990a0597 (commit aa2be227fae8c6b76884f5975a6257bb20397439 there).
 Regenerated against 0.7.0-1ubuntu2 so that it applies without fuzz: the
 soft_simple.cpp context differs in 0.7.0 ("auto const &algo"); the added
 code is unchanged.
